  "content": [
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Standard Form"
    },
    {
      "type": "formula",
      "text": "ax² + bx + c = 0  (where a ≠ 0)"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Quadratic Formula"
    },
    {
      "type": "formula",
      "text": "x = (-b ± √(b² - 4ac)) / 2a"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Discriminant (D)"
    },
    {
      "type": "formula",
      "text": "D = b² - 4ac"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "D > 0 → Two distinct real roots",
        "D = 0 → Two equal real roots (repeated root)",
        "D < 0 → No real roots (complex roots)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Vieta's Formulas (Relationship between roots and coefficients)"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "Sum of roots: α + β = -b/a",
        "Product of roots: α × β = c/a"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Methods to Solve"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "1. Factorisation — split middle term",
        "2. Completing the square",
        "3. Quadratic formula",
        "4. Graphical method"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Factorisation Method — Steps"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "Step 1: Write in standard form ax² + bx + c = 0",
        "Step 2: Find two numbers p, q such that p + q = b and p × q = ac",
        "Step 3: Split bx as px + qx",
        "Step 4: Factorise by grouping",
        "Step 5: Set each factor = 0 and solve"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "example",
      "title": "Example: Solve x² - 5x + 6 = 0",
      "steps": [
        "Find p, q: p + q = -5, p × q = 6 → p = -2, q = -3",
        "x² - 2x - 3x + 6 = 0",
        "x(x - 2) - 3(x - 2) = 0",
        "(x - 2)(x - 3) = 0",
        "x = 2 or x = 3"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Important Points to Remember"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "A quadratic equation has at most 2 roots",
        "If one root is rational, the other is also rational (for rational coefficients)",
        "If one root is irrational (a + √b), the other is its conjugate (a - √b)",
        "The graph of a quadratic is a parabola"
      ]
    }
  ]
}
